title: ch2_coffee_math
---
Unpaid CEO: Before you pour a single latte, give me one cup. Not to drink. To count. #line:ch2_coffee_math_01
Unpaid CEO: Beans, milk, lid, sleeve, the cup itself. What does one cup really cost you? #line:ch2_coffee_math_02
-> Count every cent with him. #line:ch2_coffee_math_03
    <<choose "count">>
    Unpaid CEO: A dollar twenty. Now you know what four dollars is really worth. #line:ch2_coffee_math_04
-> Just sell more, the math will follow. #line:ch2_coffee_math_05
    <<choose "skip">>
    Unpaid CEO: Volume hides mistakes. For a while. #line:ch2_coffee_math_06
===

title: ch2_coffee_inspector
---
A city inspector in a reflective vest circles your cart twice and taps the expired sticker on the window. #line:ch2_coffee_inspector_01
Your mobile vending permit renewal is three weeks late. #line:ch2_coffee_inspector_02
-> Pay the late fee and renew today. #line:ch2_coffee_inspector_03
    <<choose "pay">>
    The inspector nods. A clean sticker goes on the glass. #line:ch2_coffee_inspector_04
-> Argue that the office never sent a reminder. #line:ch2_coffee_inspector_05
    <<choose "argue">>
    You win the argument and lose two days of sales while the cart sits closed. #line:ch2_coffee_inspector_06
===

title: ch2_coffee_oatmilk
---
Every third customer asks the same thing. Do you have oat milk? #line:ch2_coffee_oatmilk_01
A carton costs you about forty cents per drink. The café across the street charges seventy-five cents extra. #line:ch2_coffee_oatmilk_02
-> Add oat milk for seventy-five cents extra. #line:ch2_coffee_oatmilk_03
    <<choose "charge">>
    The line gets longer. So does the list of things you have to keep in stock. #line:ch2_coffee_oatmilk_04
-> Offer it free to win the regulars. #line:ch2_coffee_oatmilk_05
    <<choose "free">>
    People love it. Your margin feels it every single cup. #line:ch2_coffee_oatmilk_06
-> Keep the menu simple. #line:ch2_coffee_oatmilk_07
    <<choose "simple">>
    Fewer cartons, fewer decisions, a few customers walking past. #line:ch2_coffee_oatmilk_08
===

title: ch2_coffee_loyalty
---
A nurse who buys two coffees every morning holds up a punch card from a chain store. #line:ch2_coffee_loyalty_01
Ten stamps and the next one is free. You don't do that, she says. Should you? #line:ch2_coffee_loyalty_02
-> Print punch cards. Tenth coffee free. #line:ch2_coffee_loyalty_03
    <<choose "card">>
    Free coffee costs a dollar twenty. A regular who stays a year is worth far more. #line:ch2_coffee_loyalty_04
-> No discounts. Quality speaks for itself. #line:ch2_coffee_loyalty_05
    <<choose "no">>
    She still buys. Her coworkers try the chain. #line:ch2_coffee_loyalty_06
===

title: ch2_coffee_rosa_beans
---
Rosa: I roast in Red Hook. Better beans than your bulk bags, honestly. Twenty percent more per pound. #line:ch2_coffee_rosa_beans_01
Rosa: Your customers will taste it. Your accountant will notice it. #line:ch2_coffee_rosa_beans_02
-> Switch to Rosa's beans. #line:ch2_coffee_rosa_beans_03
    <<choose "switch">>
    Rosa: Good choice. I deliver Tuesdays. Don't make me wait at the curb. #line:ch2_coffee_rosa_beans_04
-> Stay with the cheap bags for now. #line:ch2_coffee_rosa_beans_05
    <<choose "stay">>
    Rosa: Your call. My number doesn't change. #line:ch2_coffee_rosa_beans_06
===

title: ch2_coffee_rain
---
A week of cold rain. The subway stairs are empty, and so is your tip jar. #line:ch2_coffee_rain_01
-> Move the cart under the train overpass. #line:ch2_coffee_rain_02
    <<choose "move">>
    Wet commuters find you. Your shoes never dry. #line:ch2_coffee_rain_03
-> Close early and rest. #line:ch2_coffee_rain_04
    <<choose "rest">>
    You sleep ten hours. The cart sleeps too. #line:ch2_coffee_rain_05
===
